# Publish mark-api + mark-ui on Irancell-T3

Date: 2026-08-13

## Stacks

| Stack | Domain | Backend | Image |
|-------|--------|---------|-------|
| mark | mark-api.xaigrok.ir | mark-api:8130 | mark-api:latest |
| mark-ui | mark.xaigrok.ir | mark-ui:80 | mark-ui:latest |

## Deploy

- Packaged both repos (Dockerfile, compose, `.armin/docker-scripts/`)
- API image built locally and loaded on T3; first `compose up` failed with `resource temporarily unavailable`
- Cause: `kernel.threads-max` was 24426 and the host had ~24397 threads, mostly ~22398 zombie `timeout` processes under SoftEther `vpnserver` in `mullvad-1`
- Runtime fix (no VPN restart): `sudo sysctl -w kernel.threads-max=131072`
- Then `docker start mark-api` succeeded; `/health` → `{"status":"ok"}`
- UI image built locally, uploaded, compose started on `t3-net` (`mark-ui` Up)
- HAProxy SNI + Host routes added; `docker kill -s HUP haproxy`
- Certbot deploy hook extended for `mark.xaigrok.ir` and `mark-api.xaigrok.ir` (SAN mirror)

## TLS (Let's Encrypt)

- **Not issued.** Public DNS is still NXDOMAIN for both names
- Authoritative NS for `xaigrok.ir`: `ns1`–`ns6.irancellcloud.com`
- `lexmora.xaigrok.ir` still resolves to `2.144.27.74`
- Live SNI for `mark.xaigrok.ir` currently presents an unrelated cert (`CN=aipedia.xaigrok.ir`) until LE PEMs exist
- SoftEther `ovpbackup.xaigrok.ir` passthrough OK (`CN=d27332175071`)

## Verify (via `--resolve` to 127.0.0.1)

- `https://mark.xaigrok.ir/` → 200 (HTML)
- `https://mark-api.xaigrok.ir/health` → 200 `{"status":"ok"}`

## Warnings

- Let's Encrypt HTTP-01 cannot run until A records `mark` and `mark-api` → `2.144.27.74` exist on Irancell Cloud DNS
- SoftEther zombie `timeout` leak will fill `threads-max` again; `kernel.threads-max` raise is runtime-only (lost on reboot)
- Do not restart `mullvad-1` / SoftEther without explicit approval (VPN users)
